.TH ECL-TRACK 1 "2026-09-23" "ecl-client 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ecl-track \- record the steps of an operation as linked ECL logbook entries
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ecl-track start
.B \-\-op
.I ID
.B \-\-title
.I TEXT
.RI [ BODY ]
.RI [ ECL-POST-OPTIONS ]
.br
.B ecl-track step
.B \-\-op
.I ID
.B \-\-name
.I TEXT
.RB [ \-\-status " ok|fail|warn|info|skip]"
.RI [ BODY ]
.RI [ ECL-POST-OPTIONS ]
.br
.B ecl-track end
.B \-\-op
.I ID
.RB [ \-\-status " ok|fail|aborted|partial]"
.RI [ BODY ]
.br
.B ecl-track flush
.B \-\-op
.I ID
.br
.B ecl-track status
.B \-\-op
.I ID
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ecl-track
turns a multi-step operation (an upgrade, a calibration campaign, a
deployment) into a thread of ECL entries:
.TP
.B start
posts
.BI "[" ID "] START: " TITLE
and records its entry ID as the operation's parent. The
.I ECL-POST-OPTIONS
given here (instance, category, tags, form, auth) are saved and reused by
every later call.
.TP
.B step
posts
.BI "[" ID "] step " N ": " NAME " \-\- " STATUS
with
.B related
set to the parent entry. Extra options (for example
.BR \-\-attachment )
apply to this entry only.
.TP
.B end
posts
.BI "[" ID "] END \-\- " STATUS
with a generated table of all steps and their entry IDs, and closes the
operation.
.TP
.B flush
retries queued posts that failed earlier. Steps queued before the parent
existed are linked to it when flushed.
.TP
.B status
prints the state file.
.PP
Each body gets a footer with UTC time, host, user, working directory and
.B git describe
output, unless
.B \-\-no\-context
is given.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-op " ID"
Operation identifier, 1\(en128 characters of
.BR [A\-Za\-z0\-9._\-] .
Use something unique and dated, for example
.BR daq\-fw\-upgrade\-2026\-09\-23 .
.TP
.BI \-\-dir " PATH"
State directory. Default
.B $ECL_TRACK_DIR
or
.IR ./.ecl\-track .
.TP
.BI \-\-ecl\-post " PATH"
Path to
.BR ecl-post (1).
Default
.BR $ECL_POST ,
then
.BR PATH ,
then
.I ../build/ecl-post
relative to this script.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-text " " \fITEXT\fR
Entry body.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-text\-file " " \fIPATH\fR
Read the body from
.IR PATH ;
.B \-
reads standard input.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-context
Omit the context footer.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print XML and post nothing. On
.BR start ,
marks the whole operation as a dry run so later calls are also dry runs.
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Exit 1 if the post fails (the entry is still queued).
.TP
.B \-\-force
.RB ( start )
Overwrite an existing state file for
.IR ID .
.PP
.BR \-\-password ", " \-\-subject ", " \-\-text ", " \-\-text\-file " and " \-\-related
cannot be passed through to
.BR ecl-post .
.SH FAILURE HANDLING
By default a failed post prints a warning, is queued in the state file, and
.B ecl-track
exits 0. This is deliberate: an ECL outage must not abort the operation being
recorded. Check for queued entries with
.B status
and send them with
.BR flush .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR ECL_USERNAME ", " ECL_PASSWORD ", " ECL_AUTH ", " ECL_INSTANCE ", " ECL_CATEGORY
are read by
.BR ecl-post (1).
.B ECL_TRACK_DIR
sets the state directory;
.B ECL_POST
sets the ecl-post path.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success (or failure queued without
.BR \-\-strict ),
1 post failed with
.B \-\-strict
or entries remain after
.BR flush ,
2 usage error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.IB state-dir / ID .json
Operation state: saved ecl-post options, parent entry ID, entries, queue.
Contains entry bodies but never passwords.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
export ECL_USERNAME=automation-account ECL_AUTH=password
read \-rs ECL_PASSWORD; export ECL_PASSWORD
OP=daq\-fw\-upgrade\-$(date +%F)

ecl-track start \-\-op $OP \-\-title 'DTC firmware upgrade to v4.2' \e
    \-i mu2e \-c Sandbox \-t 'Plan: stop run, flash 6 DTCs, verify.'
ecl-track step \-\-op $OP \-\-name 'Run stopped' \-t 'Run 105123 ended.'
flash_all.sh 2>&1 | tee flash.log
ecl-track step \-\-op $OP \-\-name 'Flash DTCs' \-\-status ok \e
    \-\-attachment flash.log=flash.log \-t 'All 6 DTCs report v4.2.'
ecl-track end \-\-op $OP \-\-status ok
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ecl-post (1),
.BR ecl (3),
.BR ecl_client (3)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman <anorman@fnal.gov>
